  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reviewing Social Architecture Approach in Rohingya Camps and Host Community</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a an action research based project . After we implement the social architecture approach in the context of such a protected crisis, with the backing of an innovation fund, we would like to:   - Evaluation/review of the existing Social Architecture (SA) structure, use, and impact  - documenting successes and challenges    - Adapt/tweak the SA approach to the current context in Bangladesh  - Design and construct an experimental prototype structure for field testing based on the learnings of the review  Since there is not always availability of time, funding, and relevant professionals, also sometimes, references of existing knowledge have to be followed (For example; Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) sector approved latrine design, existing design the community uses, or availability of land in homestead) the team had to start working from a previously drawn line.</narrative>
  </description>
